{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ימותון", :translit "yamutun", :gloss "they die"} {:he "כמות כל האדם ימותון והארץ כבגד תבלה ויושביה כמו כן ימותון", :translit "k'mot kol ha-adam yamutun v'ha-aretz k'beged tivlah v'yoshveha k'mo khen yamutun", :gloss "like the death of all men they die and the earth like a garment is consumed and its inhabitants like so they die"} {:he "תבלה ויושביה", :translit "tivlah v'yoshveha", :gloss "is consumed and its inhabitants"} {:he "ימותון", :translit "yamutun", :gloss "they die"} {:he "יבלעו הם תחתם", :translit "yivla'u hem takhtam", :gloss "they are swallowed beneath it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ימותון"]}], :frame {:text "The word ימותון occurs twice in this verse, once at the beginning of the phrase and once at the end, forming an inclusio around the imagery of the earth being consumed like a garment (Isaiah 51:6). The Ba'al HaTurim reads the juxtaposition as indicating that the rebels are swallowed into the earth itself.", :sources ["Numbers 16:29" "Isaiah 51:6"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ופקודת", :translit "uf'kudat", :gloss "and the appointment of"} {:he "ופקודת משמרת", :translit "uf'kudat mishmeret", :gloss "and the appointment of the watch"} {:he "ופקודת אלעזר בן אהרן", :translit "uf'kudat el'azar ben aharon", :gloss "and the appointment of Elazar son of Aaron"} {:he "פקודת אלעזר", :translit "f'kudat el'azar", :gloss "appointment of Elazar"} {:he "ופקודת כל האדם וגו'", :translit "uf'kudat kol ha-adam v'gomer", :gloss "and the appointment of all men etc."}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ופקודת" "ופקודת משמרת" "ופקודת אלעזר בן אהרן"]} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking the three occurrences of ופקודת thematically: Korah sought Elazar's priestly appointment, so the verse reciprocates with ופקודת כל האדם."}], :frame {:text "Korah's rebellion is described as a challenge to the priestly appointment of Aaron's house. Elazar son of Aaron is given charge of the Levites in Numbers 3:32, and Korah's faction contested the legitimacy of this priestly hierarchy, seeking the priesthood for themselves.", :sources ["Numbers 3:32" "Numbers 16:10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ופקודת כל האדם יפקד", :translit "uf'kudat kol ha-adam yifkod", :gloss "and the appointment of all men he will appoint"} {:he "פוקד עון אבות על בנים ועל שלשים ועל רבעים", :translit "poked avon avot al banim v'al shilshim v'al ribe'im", :gloss "visits the iniquity of fathers upon children and upon third and upon fourth generations"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between God's normal way of visiting iniquity across generations (Exodus 34:7) and the immediate punishment Moses demands for Korah's faction."}], :frame {:text "Moses demands that Korah's faction be punished immediately rather than through the normal generational mechanism described at Exodus 34:7, where God visits the iniquity of fathers upon children to the third and fourth generation. Moses frames this as a test of his prophetic legitimacy.", :sources ["Exodus 34:7" "Numbers 16:28-30"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ימותון"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ימותון", :refs ["Isaiah 51:6"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ופקודת" "ופקודת משמרת" "ופקודת אלעזר בן אהרן"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ופקודת", :refs ["Exodus 3:16" "Exodus 32:34" "Numbers 3:32" "Numbers 3:36" "Numbers 4:16" "Numbers 16:29" "1 Samuel 15:2" "2 Kings 11:18"], :n 42, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ופקודת משמרת", :refs ["Numbers 3:36"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ופקודת אלעזר בן אהרן", :refs ["Numbers 4:16"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking the three occurrences of ופקודת thematically: Korah sought Elazar's priestly appointment, so the verse reciprocates with ופקודת כל האדם.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Contrast between God's normal way of visiting iniquity across generations (Exodus 